## Delivered as one actual path

Implementation: `v2/experiments/action_executor/r27/runtime_closure`, reusing frozen
real_path code without copying large modules or changing serving product/dependencies.

- D1: Genuine installed pytest LogXML collection/report/session pipeline executes.
  Its two original declaration/serialization writes are staged in bounded memory,
  then one whole XML payload commits only on successful original writer-context close.
  Exact module-local open/os aliases restore; global OS/builtins are not patched.
  Unknown/stale/empty/oversized/serialization paths fail sticky before report/header I/O.
  XML remains2048B; larger suites DENY. Two source writes→one physical final payload
  is explicit, not a claim of identical original write-attempt accounting.
- D2: Genuine stdlib fileConfig consumes unchanged original Alembic ini and configures
  the real StreamHandler/formatter/terminator. Whole rendered records≤512B route to
  the owner. Old live handler registries are protected from stdlib shutdown; detached
  working lists prevent in-place mutations destroying old handler/filter aliases.
  Success/fault controls check exact aliases and contents, caches, levels/disabled/
  propagate, streams, cold identities and shared logging lock. Sink errors propagate,
  not swallowed/native traceback fallback. Actual Alembic/migration env is pinned
  and prepared only, not run or replaced by a fake module.
- D3: Actual original source/executable-bound `/bin/df -k /` runs read-only through
  whole concurrent EOF endpoints, alongside fixed-child fault controls. Disk4096B/
  control2048B limits remain. Source mismatch, overflow, nonzero, repeated cancellation,
  active seal and cleanup faults preserve raw/primary/ownership semantics. Reap and
  named task absence are observed before loop shutdown under one first absolute10s
  cleanup. This does not prove Linux groups, descendants or arbitrary commands.
  Both local df streams, including empty stderr, count; original whole-stage eight
  disk records are not thereby proven sufficient.
- D4: One shared broker/port executes original signed fixture/genuine parser →
  genuine pytest XML → genuine fileConfig LogRecord → actual host df → close/recovery.
  Whole effect entry remains self-DENY; no SQL publication/HTTP observations substituted.
- D5: One frozen addition and actual source/dependency identities, combined controls,
  project health, retained failures and independent Main/Reviewer verification.

Reused packet seals witness the frozen real_path source set. The external addition
candidate/binding separately binds new code before/after; packet alone is not full
addition/runtime certification. Cooperative owned-source ports are not a universal
OS/native-FD/hostile same-UID sandbox.

