## Important full-runtime gaps found, not hidden

Operative files/PRE records stay **32/32**. Earlier96/PRE64 is NOT_ADOPTED and
insufficient. Full source scan corrects the earlier incomplete53-record premise:

| Conditional topology | Lifetime filenames | Source-cap records incl closure | Hypothetical serializer bytes |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| HTTP historical63 +seed5 +marker1 | 69 | Not a full-stage proof | 10,832 |
| PRE launcher nominal | 125 | 76 (75producer+1closure) | 15,510 |
| PRE one active stop | 128 | Path-dependent | 15,806 maximum |
| PRE all-stop union | 155 | Not one simultaneous execution | 18,341 |

The all-stop union exceeds16KiB; mutually exclusive branches need not coexist.
These forecasts use actual serialization with hypothetical enlarged source inventory,
not an actual sealed manifest/universal upper bound. Overwrites/interleaving/error
ranges and original PRE test/temp/native/basetemp writers are excluded/unqualified.
Repeated sample/journal/mutation copies cannot be assumed to fit final_samples1 or
ephemeral16×65KiB. No output dropping, reclassification, splitting, empty receipt,
scratch exclusion or count-only increase supplies full fit.

Twenty families/aggregate10MiB/metadata16KiB/no-refund physical-copy semantics,
old load/deadline/thresholds are unchanged. Missing host Alembic/httpx/fastapi/redis
and listed transitive/runtime dependencies are not installed or faked; presence probes
are filesystem-only, not importability/version qualification. XML/fileConfig local
seams are verified despite inherited generic blocker labels; full PRE/migration still
pending. Linux groups, physical SQL, live fixture/owned databases, PG/container df,
SQL/admin/migrations/HTTP/load/power-loss and full serving build remain NOT_RUN.
Preflight marker field only declares batch nonconsumption, not live marker absence.

